#: includes/class-welcome.php:145
msgid "Hello, admin or developer!"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:148
msgid "Out of the box, WordPress leaves a few gaps open: anyone can find your user names, your WordPress version and the address of your login page. No, the WordPress team is not being careless 🙂 some sites need them to work. On most sites, though, they can and should be closed. That is what HelloAdmin Guard does. Every gap has its own switch, so you decide what to close and what to leave open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:149
msgid "Good to know"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:151
msgid "Nothing is on until you turn it on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:152
msgid "Every switch tells you what it does, what may stop working and how to undo it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:153
msgid "The plugin is free and will stay free: no Pro version, no account, no data sent anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:154
msgid "Every new version closes more gaps, so keep the plugin updated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:156
msgid "Not sure where to start? Turn switches on one at a time and check your site after each one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:160
msgid "Got it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-welcome.php:166
msgid "Hide the welcome message"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-backups.php:34
msgid "Block backups and database dumps"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-backups.php:43
msgid "The server answers 404 for database dumps and backups (.sql, .sql.gz, .sqlite, .db, .bak, .old, .orig, .save, .wpress, files ending with ~), archives in the site root and in the content folder (backup.zip, site.tar.gz), every file whose name starts with wp-config (wp-config.txt, wp-config.old, wp-config.php.save; WordPress still reads wp-config.php from the disk), Duplicator installer.php leftovers and the backup folders of UpdraftPlus, All-in-One WP Migration, Duplicator and BackWPup. A file like this left after a move gives away the whole site and its database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-backups.php:52
msgid "Download links to archives in the site root or the content folder and to .sql or .bak files, if you share them on purpose. Archives in the uploads folder stay open. Backup plugins keep working: they read their folders from PHP, not over the web."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-core-internals.php:34
msgid "Close internal WordPress folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-core-internals.php:43
msgid "The server answers 404 when someone opens PHP files from wp-admin/includes, wp-includes (top level), wp-includes/theme-compat or the TinyMCE language files directly. WordPress only loads them from inside; opened from the browser, some print errors with full server paths. These are the rules from the WordPress hardening guide."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-core-internals.php:52
msgid "Multisite networks that still serve files through wp-includes/ms-files.php (networks created before WordPress 3.5)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-dev-files.php:34
msgid "Block developer and build files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-dev-files.php:43
msgid "The server answers 404 for package and build files (composer.json, composer.lock, package.json, package-lock.json, yarn.lock, gulpfile.js, webpack and Vite configs), deploy files (Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, wp-cli.yml, deploy.php, Makefile), php.ini copies, source maps (.map) and text files of plugins, themes and translations (.md, .txt, .po, .mo, .pot, .yml, .lock) inside the content folder, plus .md, .yml and .sh files in the site root. They list exact versions of libraries with known holes and describe the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-dev-files.php:52
msgid "Browser developer tools stop showing the original source of minified scripts. Uploads are not touched. robots.txt, ads.txt and other .txt files in the site root stay open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-hidden-files.php:34
msgid "Block hidden files (.git, .env)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-hidden-files.php:43
msgid "The server answers 404 for every file and folder whose name starts with a dot: .git (the whole code history), .env (database passwords and API keys), .htpasswd, .svn, .DS_Store, editor backups like .wp-config.php.swp. These show up when a site is deployed with Git or copied from a computer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-hidden-files.php:52
msgid "Nothing on a normal site. /.well-known/ stays open: SSL certificates and app links need it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-logs.php:34
msgid "Block logs and diagnostic pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-logs.php:43
msgid "The server answers 404 for log files (debug.log, error_log, any .log), WooCommerce logs (uploads/wc-logs), Wordfence data (wflogs), forgotten test pages in the site root (phpinfo.php, info.php, test.php) and the Apache status pages (/server-status, /server-info). They show server paths, the hosting user name, versions of PHP and libraries, and sometimes errors from payment gateways."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-block-logs.php:52
msgid "Opening a log or a test page in the browser on purpose: read logs over SFTP or in the hosting panel instead. Logging itself keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-app-passwords.php:33
msgid "Turn off Application Passwords"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-app-passwords.php:40
msgid "Application Passwords let apps log in to the REST API without the login page and without two-factor login. This turns them off for all users and hides the section in user profiles. Passwords that already exist are kept, they just stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-app-passwords.php:47
msgid "The WordPress mobile app on sites without Jetpack, Zapier, Make and other services connected with an application password, and your own scripts that publish through the REST API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-app-passwords.php:54
msgid "Turn this off and save. The existing application passwords work again; nobody needs to create new ones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-file-editor.php:37
msgid "Turn off the file editor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-file-editor.php:44
msgid "Removes Appearance > Theme File Editor and Plugins > Plugin File Editor. Anyone who gets into an admin account can no longer put their own PHP code into the site from the browser."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-file-editor.php:51
msgid "Quick code edits from wp-admin: change theme and plugin files over SFTP, SSH or Git instead. The Site Editor, the Customizer and Additional CSS keep working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-file-editor.php:58
msgid "Turn this off and save. The editors come back at once; nothing is changed in wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-listing.php:34
msgid "Turn off folder listings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-listing.php:43
msgid "Adds \"Options -Indexes\": when a folder has no index file, the server answers 403 instead of a list of all files in it. WordPress puts an empty index.php only into wp-content, plugins and themes, so on many hosts /wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ shows every uploaded file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-listing.php:52
msgid "Nothing on the site. On a few hosts .htaccess may not change Options: then the home page answers with an error, the plugin puts the old file back and keeps this setting off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-xmlrpc.php:33
msgid "Turn off XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-xmlrpc.php:40
msgid "Every request to /xmlrpc.php gets a 403 answer, so bots cannot try many passwords in one request through system.multicall. The X-Pingback header and the RSD link in the page source are removed too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-xmlrpc.php:47
msgid "Jetpack and other services that connect to the site through XML-RPC, old desktop and mobile blogging apps, and pingbacks from other blogs. The WordPress mobile app works through the REST API and is not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-disable-xmlrpc.php:54 includes/features/class-user-enumeration.php:53
msgid "Turn this off and save. Nothing is deleted or changed in the database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hide-version-files.php:35
msgid "Hide files that show versions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hide-version-files.php:44
msgid "The server answers 404 for readme.html, license.txt, wp-config-sample.php and wp-links-opml.php in the site root, for readme, changelog and license files inside plugin and theme folders, and for wp-admin/install.php, setup-config.php and upgrade.php (upgrade.php stays open for logged-in users). WordPress does not load plugins on the install and upgrade pages, so they show the version even when it is hidden elsewhere. Bots read all these files to find sites with known holes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hide-version-files.php:53
msgid "Nothing on the site itself: WordPress and browsers do not need these files. Installing WordPress again over this site needs the setting off. Online scanners that guess plugin versions from readme.txt will see less."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hide-wp-version.php:34
msgid "Hide the WordPress version"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hide-wp-version.php:41
msgid "Removes the WordPress version from the generator tag in the page source and feeds, and from ?ver= in the links to core scripts and styles. Also removes the X-Powered-By header with the PHP version. This only slows bots down; keeping WordPress and PHP updated is the real fix."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hide-wp-version.php:48
msgid "Nothing on the site itself. Online scanners and some SEO tools will no longer show your WordPress version. Plugin versions in their own file links are not changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hide-wp-version.php:55
msgid "Turn this off and save. If a page looks broken right after that, clear the page cache once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hsts.php:38
msgid "HTTPS only (HSTS)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hsts.php:47
msgid "Adds the Strict-Transport-Security header: after the first visit, browsers open your site only over HTTPS for one year, even if someone types http:// or a public Wi-Fi tries to send them to the plain version. Sent only when the page itself is loaded over HTTPS. Subdomains are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hsts.php:56
msgid "If the SSL certificate expires or HTTPS stops working, visitors who have been to the site cannot open it at all, there is no \"continue anyway\" button. Turn this on only when HTTPS works on every page and the certificate renews by itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-hsts.php:65
msgid "Turn this off and save: the header is no longer sent. Browsers that already got it keep using HTTPS until the year runs out, this cannot be taken back from the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:50
msgid "Custom login URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:57
msgid "Moves the login page to your own address. /wp-login.php and /wp-admin/ show a 404 page to visitors who are not logged in, so bots stop finding the login form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:64
msgid "Bookmarks and saved passwords for the old login page. Plugins or apps that log in through /wp-login.php directly. Another plugin that also changes the login URL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:71
msgid "Turn this off and save. If you forgot the new address and cannot log in, rename the folder wp-content/plugins/helloadmin-guard over FTP or in the hosting file manager: the plugin stops and /wp-login.php works again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:114
msgid "Login address"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: login page URL.
#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:119
#, php-format
msgid "Letters, numbers and dashes, at least 4 characters. Your login page: %s. Bookmark it after saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:140
msgid "The login address must be at least 4 characters long."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:142
msgid "This login address is reserved by WordPress or too easy to guess. Choose another one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:144
msgid "A page or post already uses this address. Choose another one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-login-url.php:270
msgid "The requested URL was not found on this server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-no-php-in-uploads.php:35
msgid "No PHP in the uploads folder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-no-php-in-uploads.php:44
msgid "The server answers 404 to any PHP file in the uploads folder. If a weak plugin or form lets someone upload a PHP file there, it cannot be opened from the browser."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-no-php-in-uploads.php:53
msgid "A rare plugin that keeps its own PHP scripts in the uploads folder and opens them from the browser. Images, PDFs and other uploads work as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:33
msgid "Security headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:40
msgid "Adds four headers: X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff (browsers do not guess file types), X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN (other sites cannot show your pages in a frame), Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin (other sites see only your domain, not full URLs) and Permissions-Policy (no camera or microphone, location only for your own pages)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:47
msgid "Showing your pages inside a frame on another domain, for example a landing page builder or a partner site. Embedded widgets from other sites that ask for the camera, microphone or location. Your own pages, the editor and the Customizer are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:54
msgid "Turn this off and save. Browsers drop these headers on the next page load. If the server or another plugin also sends them, those copies stay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-user-enumeration.php:32
msgid "Hide user names"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-user-enumeration.php:39
msgid "Visitors who are not logged in can no longer get user names from /?author=1, the REST API user list (/wp-json/wp/v2/users), oEmbed author links and the users sitemap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-user-enumeration.php:46
msgid "Apps or scripts that read the user list through the REST API without logging in. Author pages drop out of wp-sitemap.xml; the pages themselves keep working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-user-enumeration.php:132
msgid "Sorry, you are not allowed to list users."
msgstr ""
